Used product control encompasses the systems and processes for assessing, sorting, documenting, and directing recovered products toward appropriate end-of-life pathways. Effective control ensures that repairable products go to refurbishment, those unsuitable for reuse go to material recovery, and damaged or unsafe items are properly managed. Strong used product control maximizes recovery value while preventing poor-quality products from damaging brand reputation in secondary markets. Design impacts control feasibility through modularity, material identification, and condition standardization.